The service was returning the incoming DTO as-is. Populate an id (or map/save to a repository) so the returned object contains all fields. Updated `backend/src/main/java/dev/jclawlor/FitnessGoals/serviceImpl/MealServiceImpl.java`:

```java
package dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.serviceImpl;

import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.dto.MealDto;
import dev.jclawlor.FitnessGoals.service.MealService;

@Service
public class MealServiceImpl implements MealService {

    @Override
    public MealDto addMeal(MealDto mealDto) {
        // simulate persistence by assigning an id if missing so the returned DTO includes it
        if (mealDto.getId() == null) {
            mealDto.setId(Math.abs(System.currentTimeMillis()));
        }
        // return the full DTO (all fields from the request are preserved)
        return mealDto;
    }

    @Override
    public MealDto updateMeal(Long id, MealDto mealDto) {
        // ensure the DTO has the updated id
        mealDto.setId(id);
        return mealDto;
    }
}
```
